  "body": "**Stacked on #382** (Machines pane, browse + validate): this branch carries #382's commits plus a merge of current main. Merge #382 first; this PR's own diff is then the last two commits (`cb293f30`, `35cfa074`) plus the merge.\n\n## What changed\n- The Machines pane's detail view gets a **\"Use for this setup\"** button under the validation verdict. Clicking it queues `CommandKind::UseCatalogueMachine(MachineSource)`.\n- It follows main's per-setup machine route (#343): `State::mount_catalogue` -> `route_machine(MachineVerb::Mount(..))`. If the active setup owns its machine, the selected machine replaces it (`SetSetupMachine`); otherwise the document's machine changes (`LoadMachine`). One undo step either way.\n- Validation is re-run at assignment: `machine::library::read_for_assign` re-reads the built-in text or file, runs `validate_text`, and refuses with the first refusal, so a refused machine never mounts even if the command is queued directly. Shared by `LoadMachine::from_catalogue`, the new `SetSetupMachine::from_catalogue` and the UI route.\n- The button is disabled with the reason shown under it and on hover: \"fails validation - <first refusal> (and N more)\" or \"it is already this setup's machine\" (reads `machine::of`, the active setup's effective machine).\n- `MachineSource::mount_path()` mounts built-ins at `built-in: <name>`, the path the Setup pane's Library list already uses.\n- Decision only (no code): the `machine_editor.rs` window becomes the pane's edit mode when the editing slice (#383) lands.\n\n## Readings\nDebug, M5 Mac. `scripts/gate.sh quick` (all camcraft-app + camcraft-ui suites): 1734 passed, 4 failed - all known reds on main (`setup_stock_source::a_new_block_after_a_flip…` #415; GPU headless trio). Clippy `-D warnings` clean on app + ui.\n\n## Pinning tests\n- App `crates/app/tests/machine_assign.rs`: `assigning_a_catalogue_machine_does_undoes_and_redoes`, `a_refused_machine_cannot_be_assigned_and_says_why`, `a_setup_with_its_own_machine_takes_the_catalogue_machine`.\n- UI lib `egui_app::tests::machines_pane`: `use_for_this_setup_assigns_the_selected_machine_and_undo_restores_it`, `a_refused_machine_cannot_be_assigned_and_names_why`, `use_for_this_setup_replaces_an_own_machine_and_leaves_the_document_alone`.\n\n## Not exercised\nNo hand GUI run yet (**draft until the GUI check**); Ctrl+Y redo only at app level; disabled-hover text not asserted. Posted G-code unchanged (machines mount through the existing commands).\n\nDecisions: `docs/decisions/384-machines-use-for-setup.md`.\n\nChangelog: The Machines pane's \"Use for this setup\" assigns the selected machine to the active setup (its own machine or the document's), undoable; a machine that fails validation can't be assigned and says why\n\nFixes #384\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
